   253	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   254	    """
   255	    Fill hollow sprites by decoding a diagonal edge legend in the opposite direction.
   256	
   257	    Input structure:
   258	    - Background is the dominant border color. Several hollow sprites sit on that background.
   259	    - A sparse palette legend appears as a single diagonal chain of colored cells starting on
   260	      the top or bottom edge. The visible edge-to-interior order is intentionally misleading:
   261	      consecutive displayed cells are not the intended `(border, fill)` pairs.
   262	
   263	    Rule:
   264	    - Detect the diagonal legend, reverse the chain order, and then read the reversed sequence
   265	      two cells at a time as `(border color, fill color)` pairs.
   266	    - Find enclosed background regions that do not touch the global grid boundary.
   267	    - For each such region, measure the most common adjacent border color; if that color is a
   268	      decoded palette key, fill the region with the mapped palette value.
   269	
   270	    Key insight:
   271	    - The legend must be read along a diagonal, but not in the intuitive boundary-inward
   272	      direction. Reversing the entire diagonal sequence is what reveals which colors are keys
   273	      and which are fills.
   274	    """
